URL: https://github.com/KadNaf/PGA-cmdr
Description:
    PGA-cmdr is an interactive 'shiny' application for population genetics
    analyses of multilocus individual genotype data from codominant markers
    (microsatellites, allozymes, SNPs). It covers data import and
    formatting, allele frequencies and missing data, observed and expected
    heterozygosity, F-statistics (FIS, FST, FIT) following Weir and
    Cockerham (1984) <doi:10.1111/j.1558-5646.1984.tb05657.x>, and gene diversities (HS, HT)
    following Nei and Chesser (1983) <doi:10.1111/j.1469-1809.1983.tb00993.x>.
    Analyses include local and global panmixia tests, population subdivision with a G-based test of
    genotypic differentiation, pairwise linkage disequilibrium tests, null
    allele frequency estimation with the ENA correction of Chapuis and
    Estoup (2007) <doi:10.1093/molbev/msl191>, and isolation by distance
    using the regression of Rousset (1997) <doi:10.1093/genetics/145.4.1219> and a Mantel test. 
    Confidence intervals are obtained by bootstrap over individuals, sub-samples or
    loci, and p-values by Monte Carlo permutation, computed in parallel in
    C++ via 'Rcpp' and 'OpenMP'. All computations run locally and no data
    leave the user's computer.
